{
 "case": "CAP-11",
 "says": "A person binds this device's key and the checkout and registers the repository's decisions source, founds a Team alone (team.found), registers the Team's decision source, and selects one transcript span permitting results in the repository and the Team (source.observe). The owner admits the capture at generation 7 (access.admission.decide) and saves it as a Team-source draft stating its widening from the repository with the founder's grant as authority (source.capture.record). A candidate is stored (memory.candidate.store) and presented unchanged (memory.candidate.read); while its promotion is admitted against that head, the Team resets its own rights on the source, moving the head, so promotion is refused stale_base on completion - present and promote both reevaluate the fixed target's current state, not admission-time state. Six later changes must each stop a late extraction being saved, redirected or revived, none writing anything: an executing extraction for the repository's source is cancelled by request id (operation.cancel); querying it returns withdrawn with no output, still true much later under a moved access generation; the transcript file is rewritten, a second observation reads other bytes, and the same capture naming the first, now-superseded observation is refused working_bytes_moved when resealed; the Team's policy moves to version 2, and the same capture naming the old policy digest is refused policy_superseded; the Team is archived, and the same capture for it is refused team_archived; and a capture admitted at generation 7 arrives after sign-out (generation 8): refused access_signed_out and access_generation_moved, and readmission answers not_admitted with the same two gaps. No late result attaches to another request, target, the changed bytes or the superseded policy.",
